{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The wicked</b> — [the word] 'height' is joined to 'anger,' because there is no height before it, and there is no doubt that haughtiness in the heart is only a matter of the manifest." "<b>He does not seek</b> — [i.e.] apart from [this], and [the bet] is missing from the word 'all his thoughts' [כל זמותיו]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The Hebrew of comment [0] is elliptical; 'joined to anger' likely refers to the prosodic or syntactic linkage of רשע with the following phrase involving אף, but the exact grammatical argument is compressed and obscure.", 1 "The comment is cryptic: Ibn Ezra appears to posit that בל functions as בלתי minus the letter, or that the phrase כל זמותיו should have had a prefixed bet. The syntax of the Hebrew is elliptical and the precise point is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:52.485720455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}